AIKIDO-2026-310861 (CWE-843) -- seroval-plugins: require a fixed seroval core.

The vulnerability lives in the seroval CORE package
(packages/seroval/src/core/context/deserializer.ts), fixed upstream in
seroval 1.6.2 (commit f1ffcc96d259f9b5b3d71feb262b58240c90e7b7).

seroval-plugins@1.6.7 ships only dist/ -- it does not contain deserializer.ts.
Its published peerDependency is still "seroval": "^1.0", which allows a
vulnerable 1.5.x core to remain installed. The code fix is already in
seroval 1.6.7 (devDependency is already pinned there); this patch only
tightens the peer constraint so installs cannot keep seroval < 1.6.2.

--- a/package.json
+++ b/package.json
@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@
     "vitest": "^4.1.10"
   },
   "peerDependencies": {
-    "seroval": "^1.0"
+    "seroval": ">=1.6.2"
   },
   "private": false,
   "description": "Stringify JS values",
